---
description: Never trust the client — admin gate, money, orders
alwaysApply: true
---

# Security (server is the source of truth)

Hiding a button in React is **not** authorization. A shopper who types `/admin` or forges `fetch` must still get **403** from Spring.

## Admin

- Seeded `ADMIN` only (`APP_ADMIN_EMAIL`). Signup always creates `SHOPPER`.
- `/api/admin/**` → `hasRole("ADMIN")`. Same on `@PreAuthorize` for product write and CSV import.
- SPA: after `GET /api/auth/me`, if `role !== ADMIN`, `/admin/**` redirects home. Do not skip the API check.

```text
❌ if (localStorage.role === "ADMIN") allow delete SKU
✅ API rejects SHOPPER; UI only hides the link
```

## Money and cart (no “pay less”)

- Cart body is `{ sku, qty }` only. Checkout body is empty; header `Idempotency-Key`.
- Unit price, name, line total, order total come from **locked product rows** at pay time (`BigDecimal`). Ignore any price the UI might send.
- Stock check is server-side (`SELECT FOR UPDATE`). Qty in the UI is a hint (`N available`); 409 if the client lies.

```text
❌ POST /api/checkout { total: 0.01, items: [{ price: 0 }] }
✅ POST /api/checkout + Idempotency-Key; server prices from products
```

## Orders

- No `DELETE` / `PUT` on orders. Status is written only by checkout.
- Shopper `GET /api/orders/{id}` → 404 if not owner. Admin read-only list. Snapshots on `order_items` so a later CSV cannot rewrite a receipt.
- Do not accept a client-supplied `userId` to shop as someone else; use the authenticated principal.
